   "gloss": "bad → ugly / I don't like it",
   "note": "'Rău' is the book's word for bad, but about a person it leans toward mean/evil, and about clothes it sounds odd. A garment you dislike is 'urât' (ugly), or you just say 'nu-mi place' (I don't like it). Keep rău as the opposite of bun in the abstract; reach for urât in front of a wardrobe.",
